  "name": "star-watch",
  "vibe": "A public observatory at 11pm. #0b1026 midnight indigo grounds every frame, Prata's high-contrast serif is set in pale #ece9f4, and one warm gold (#ffd97b) is reserved for whatever glows. This is the rare pack whose world runs on all seven beats: 26 stars twinkling on independent sine phases, a five-point constellation whose gold line literally draws itself across the scene, a meteor streaking down-right on a slow loop, and a lilac telescope planted bottom-left with a gold star at the eyepiece. Cards, montage tiles and stat numbers all carry a glow halo, so copy reads lit rather than printed. The camera drifts and pushes at very low magnitude, nothing snaps, and titles settle in on a drowse. Owns a gauge Ring, ticker Scroll, caret Typing pass and side-entering Notify cards. Built for planetariums, science centres, dark-sky tourism and night events.",
